Hi Corentin,

FYI, kernel build failed on

tree:   git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git master
head:   90db76e829479ef2ba1fed8f2552846015469831
commit: a979e2e2af7d5b4bb3b20f6a716c627bb23a6753 samsung-laptop: unregister ACPI video module for some well known laptops
date:   1 year, 4 months ago
config: x86_64-randconfig-c01-0721 (attached as .config)

All error/warnings:

   drivers/built-in.o: In function `samsung_init':
>> samsung-laptop.c:(.init.text+0x19f80): undefined reference to `acpi_video_unregister'

The error happens when

CONFIG_ACPI_VIDEO=m
CONFIG_SAMSUNG_LAPTOP=y

while include/acpi/video.h has this

#if (defined CONFIG_ACPI_VIDEO || defined CONFIG_ACPI_VIDEO_MODULE)
extern void acpi_video_unregister(void);
#else
static inline void acpi_video_unregister(void) { return; }
#endif

